/* DISCOVERY / derivation (CONTRIBUTION 3): the ADAPTIVE information-exploration duality, the SEQUENTIAL
   analogue of results 10 (static Cramer-Rao) and 11 (static Av+B/v rule). At round t the controller
   injects exploration variance v_t; the accumulated Fisher information about the effect is
   m_t = m0 + sum_{s<t} v_s (variance units, m0 the prior/van-Trees info). The VAN TREES (Bayesian
   Cramer-Rao) inequality bounds the Bayes risk of the effect estimate BELOW by K/m_t even for
   SEQUENTIAL/adaptive observations (ordinary CR does not apply to adaptive designs), so any schedule
   pays cumulative regret >= sum_t [A*v_t + K/m_t]. TWO DISTINCT objects, kept separate below: (i) the
   MYOPIC one-step rule v* = sqrt(K/A) - m (a one-shot terminal-estimation optimum); (ii) the RATE-OPTIMAL
   sequential SCHEDULE v_t = kappa/sqrt(t), which achieves cumulative Theta(sqrt(T)) matched by the
   sequence LOWER bound sum_t[...] >= 2*sqrt(A*K*T) - A*m0. The t^{-1/2} schedule / sqrt(T) rate / van-Trees
   sqrt(T) lower bound are KNOWN in adaptive LQR (Ziemann-Sandberg; Wagenmaker et al.); only a
   confounding-specific constant would be new, and is NOT derived here. Maxima is the source of truth. */
display2d : false$

/* per-round tradeoff at accumulated info level m (=I before this round, in variance units): exploration
   cost A*v plus the van-Trees estimation floor K/(m+v), K = C*sigma^2. */
f(v) := A*v + K/(m + v)$
print("per-round tradeoff f(v) = A*v + K/(m+v),  A = b^2+rr,  K = C*sigma^2 (van-Trees floor numerator)")$

/* optimal single-round exploration: f'(v) = A - K/(m+v)^2 = 0 => (m+v*)^2 = K/A => v* = sqrt(K/A) - m */
fp : diff(f(v), v)$
vstar : rhs(solve(fp = 0, v)[2])$
print("f'(v) =", fp, " ; optimal v* =", vstar, " = sqrt(K/A) - m")$
print("f''(v) =", ratsimp(diff(f(v), v, 2)), " > 0 : convex, v* the unique interior optimum")$

/* the SOS optimality identity (sqrt-free via (m+vs)^2 = K/A): f(v) - f(v*) = A*(v - v*)^2/(m+v) >= 0 */
gap : ratsimp( (A*v + (A*vs^2)/(m + v)) - (A*vs + (A*vs^2)/(m + vs)) )$   /* K replaced by A*(m+vs)^2, and m+vs=... */
print("f(v)-f(v*) SOS check: A*(v-vs)^2/(m+v) - gap_form =",
      ratsimp(A*(v - vs)^2/(m + v) - ((A*v + A*(m+vs)^2/(m+v)) - (A*vs + A*(m+vs)^2/(m+vs)))),
      " (0 confirms f(v)-f(v*) = A*(v-vs)^2/(m+v))")$

/* THE MYOPIC RULE (one-shot): if v could lower THIS round's floor, the one-step optimum is
   v* = max(0, sqrt(K/A) - m), decreasing in m, stopping at the threshold m >= sqrt(K/A). This is a
   terminal-estimation object -- NOT the sequential schedule (in the sequential objective v_t lowers only
   FUTURE floors, so the myopic per-round v_t is 0). Kept only to characterise the threshold. */
print("MYOPIC one-step rule v* = max(0, sqrt(K/A) - m) : distinct from the sequential schedule")$

/* THE SEQUENCE LOWER BOUND (the actual sqrt(T)): with total budget M = sum_t v_t and m_t = m0+sum_{s<t}v_s
   <= m0+M, sum_t[A*v_t + K/m_t] >= A*M + K*T/(m0+M) = A*x + K*T/x - A*m0 for x = m0+M. Reduced scalar
   objective g(x) = A*x + K*T/x is minimised at x = sqrt(K*T/A) with value 2*sqrt(A*K*T); AM-GM SOS check
   (sqrt-free with s^2 = A*K*T): A*x + K*T/x - 2*s = A*(x - s/A)^2/x >= 0. */
gAMGM : ratsimp( A*x + (s^2/A)/x - 2*s - A*(x - s/A)^2/x )$   /* K*T = s^2/A since s^2 = A*K*T */
print("sequence AM-GM SOS check: A*x + K*T/x - 2*s - A*(x-s/A)^2/x =", gAMGM,
      " (0 confirms reduced g(x) >= 2*sqrt(A*K*T); Rocq: reduced_objective_lower_bound)")$
print("=> sequential regret >= 2*sqrt(A*K*T) - A*m0 = Theta(sqrt(T)), matched by v_t = kappa/sqrt(t)")$

/* van Trees floor is ANTITONE in accumulated info: more exploration so far => lower estimation floor. */
print("van-Trees floor K/(m0 + I) is antitone in accumulated info I (Rocq: van_trees_floor_antitone)")$

/* contrast with result 11 (static): result 11 minimises A*v + B/v (single-shot, m=0), giving a CONSTANT
   v* applied every round -- which OVER-explores (keeps paying A*v after info is plentiful). The adaptive
   schedule strictly improves cumulative regret by tapering exploration to the van-Trees floor. */
print("static (result 11) v*=sqrt(B/A) applied every round over-explores; adaptive schedule tapers")$
